    {
      "id": "specification-representations",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Representations",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Representations",
        "body": "A spec is a page built from the Page Template: one import of that template, a masthead, an “At a glance” list, the eight sections as Page Section nodes and a Page Route for each example. The template’s Method assembles them into three faces, named Detail, Summary and Icon. The Detail face is the page a reader sees; the pieces themselves are hidden when browsing. The root is top left, the pieces in the interior, the faces along the bottom. Preserve existing stable IDs. The chain of faces ends in a Glyph. A face may render glyph-shaped artwork without being named Icon. It is still a face. Every authored Surface starts with at least one face and ends in its ordinary Glyph; the terminal Glyph does not replace the face.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592077147,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
